A||||3||Jncomutt||Ut Oh... Burning Oil??||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||04-29-2001||08:09 PM||||As I do more and more work to my 84 2m4 I recently purchased, I'm coming across more and more issues.  The latest issue is with blue smoke.  I just had the oil changed yesterday (first time since I bought the car, only drove it 20 miles on the old oil.)  The car never smoked before at all.  Now, only noticeable when the car is started, there is a big cloud of blue smoke.<P>Could this be because of spilled oil or because its a different brand?? (I put in Mobil 5w-30.)  Or do you thing there could be other possiblities.  The car only has 50520 Miles on it so I don't think it could be too worn.  Plus it was owned by a lady for the first 6 years driven, and the last 10 that it sat. <P>I'm gonna see if this large amount reduces over the days or gets worse, I'll keep you posted.  Thanx for any suggestions you guys may have with whats goin on here.||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||04-29-2001||09:12 PM||||If it only smokes when first started, and/or if it smokes when you drive away after prolonged idling, then your engine may have worn valve stem seals.  They're relatively easy to replace.  (Head stays on; engine stays in car.)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||04-29-2001||09:23 PM||||may be some just spilled on rear exhaust manifold rite below the fill cap. Almost all Fieros ive seen smoke pretty heavy for a second or two starting. Mine does, I dont use any oil as in having to add between changes, and I put 5000-7000 miles between changes. Fierolisas smokes the same way as mine starting and it dont use any oil either. She went to florida and back plus around town here without adding. Mine did use a little before I switched to sythetic. If its still smoking from the exhaust, a switch to the synthetic may stop it for the cost of an oil change. I pay about $25 for filter and Castrol Synthetic. If it dont stop, all your out is an extra oil change.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 04-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||04-29-2001||09:42 PM||||My experience with Synth oil in old engines would suggest that it would start them smoking. I was told by a mechanic that this is because synth contains a higher concentration of detergents... Comments?||||reg||5
